.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.streamlit/secrets.toml
tests/private/

# Statement data must never enter the repo (spec §9.2).
*.pdf
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
# No exception for tests/fixtures/. Spec §9.2 carves one out for synthetic
# generator output, but nothing writes to that directory: tests/fixtures/
# synth.py builds each statement in memory and hands the bytes straight to
# the parser. The blanket `!tests/fixtures/**` that used to sit here bought
# nothing and cost two things - it re-included tests/fixtures/__pycache__
# (confirmed with `git check-ignore -v`), and it would have re-included a
# real .csv dropped in that directory, which is the exact leak the patterns
# above exist to stop. Restore a NARROW negation here if a generator ever
# does write a file.

# SDD scratch workspace (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/
